 the Eurasian steppe.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tanguts"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tanguts.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tanguts</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Tanguts were a people of north-western China, speaking a Tibeto-Burman language, who lived in the Ordos and the Gansu corridor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/tanimoune"><span class="enc-name">Tanimoune</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Tanimoune dan Souleymane was sultan of Damagaram, with its capital at Zinder, in the mid and later 19th century, until 1884.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/taninganwe"><span class="enc-name">Taninganwe</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Taninganwe was king of the Restored Toungoo dynasty of Burma from 1714 to 1733.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tanintharyi-region"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tanintharyi-region.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tanintharyi Region</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Tanintharyi Region, historically Tenasserim, is the southernmost region of Myanmar, a long coastal strip between the Andaman Sea and the Tenasserim Hills along the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tanis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tanis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tanis</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Tanis was an ancient city in the north-eastern Nile Delta of Egypt.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tanit"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tanit.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tanit</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Tanit was the chief goddess of Carthage and the Punic world, often paired with the god Baal Hammon and called 'face of Baal'.</span></a></li></ul>
